&lt;p data-start=&quot;250&quot; data-end=&quot;799&quot;&gt;The development hereby approved shall incorporate the proposed bird box as shown on the submitted plans. The bird box shall be installed prior to first occupation of the development and maintained thereafter. The bird box shall be positioned to ensure suitability for nesting birds, with a clear flight path, at an appropriate height (generally between 3–5 metres above ground), and avoiding placement immediately above doors or windows. Where possible, the bird box should face north, east or north-east to avoid direct sunlight.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left: 15px;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;801&quot; data-end=&quot;1060&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;801&quot; data-end=&quot;812&quot;&gt;Reason:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br data-start=&quot;812&quot; data-end=&quot;815&quot;&gt;
To ensure the effective provision of nesting opportunities for birds, including swifts, sparrows and starlings, thereby supporting Hackney’s biodiversity objectives in accordance with Policy LP33 and Policy LP47 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033&lt;/p&gt;
